                  <provenance type="#m b"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_198">Eton,
                        Buckinghamshire. Royal College of the Assumption of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Contains the marginalia of Robert Elyot, fellow of Eton from c.
                        1474 until his death in January 1499 (BRUO 638). He was a prolific annotator
                        of books at Eton. Five are particularly heavily marked and were probably his
                        own, subsequently given to the college: MSS 17, 18, 34, 36, 76. (His marks
                        were discussed by N. R. Ker in The Library, 5th ser. 30 (1975), 233--7, with
                        an addendum by R. Beadle in The Library, 5th ser. 32 (1977),
                        371--2.)</p><p>In a binding by Andrew Lisley, a Winchester librarius
                        employed by the college, 1519--22; on whom see Willoughby, Collegiate
                        Churches, 129--30, 136--7.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Humphrey Gilbert (s. xvi), probably acquired
                     by him from Eton as he was educated there.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to University College by Mary Elmhurst
                     in memory of Herbert Elmhurst, scholar of the College (1670).</provenance>
               </history>
